# Regression: a DEQUE receiver's HOF result array carries the result element's
# runtime metadata, exactly as a Vector's does.
#
# THIS CELL EXISTS BECAUSE IT IS THE ONE PLACE THE FIX REASONS RATHER THAN
# MEASURES. The result element's hooks are resolved through
# `infer_fn_ptr_stores_from_types` with a hardcoded `CollectionCtorKind::Vector`
# even when the receiver is a `Deque` — on the argument that the accumulator the
# expander mints is a `gorget_array` either way, and that the resolver serves
# `Vector` and `Deque` from ONE arm at ONE set of offsets. The argument is true
# today. An argument is not a measurement, so this is the cell that notices if
# it stops being true.
#
# Self-contained on purpose: all four `drop-cust` lines land inside
# `via_deque_map`, two for the source it builds and two for the result `map`
# mints, so the expected output does not depend on scope-exit ordering in
# `main`.
#
# RED-VERIFIED against the pre-fix compiler, BOTH backends: TWO `drop-cust`
# lines, not four — the source Deque dropped its elements and the mapped
# result did not. C and `--backend=llvm` agree at two before and at four
# after, so the receiver kind is not a backend-specific path.
#
# ⚠ RUST LANE ONLY, and the reason is filed rather than hidden: the self-host
# cannot compile `Deque.map` at all — its emitted C fails with `incompatible
# types when assigning to type 'GorgetArray' from type 'int'`. That is
# `todo/t1286`, with its own durable repro; it is a lane divergence in the
# self-host's direction, not a property of this fix.
#
# ⚠ THAT is why this file sits in `self_host_gaps/` instead of at top level: a
# top-level fixture is auto-scanned into `runtime_parity_corpus`, and parking it
# here keeps this round's own inflow out of `RUNTIME_DIFF_NONMATCH_CEILING`
# (Core #9 ⊕). It moves up to top level when `todo/t1286` lands.
#
# NOT ASSERTED ASan-CLEAN — and ⚠ THE STATED REASON IS RETIRED (R50 Track E).
# It said "the closure literal leaks an 8-byte environment through
# `todo/t0953`"; measured, this fixture went from `8 byte(s) leaked in 1
# allocation(s)` to fully CLEAN, because a DEQUE receiver is name-stripped into
# the same `try_emit_vector_each_hof` site the Vector one uses and is drained
# with it. ⭐ THAT MAKES THIS A LIVE CHANGED CELL WITH NO LEAK INSTRUMENT: the
# wired test is a stdout assertion, which is structurally blind to a leak, and
# `self_host_gaps/` is out of the sanitize corpus. It is recorded as named
# omission O1 on `todo/t0953` rather than left to inference. Regenerate:
# `gg build --sanitize` on this file under
# `ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=1:exitcode=0 LSAN_OPTIONS=use_stacks=0`.

from std.collections import Deque

struct Cust:
    String s

equip Cust with Drop:
    void drop(^self):
        print("drop-cust")

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

int via_deque_map():
    Deque[Cust] src = Deque[Cust]()
    src.push(Cust(mk("aa", "bc")))
    src.push(Cust(mk("dd", "efg")))
    Deque[Cust] r = src.map((c): Cust(mk(c.s, "!")))
    return r.len()

void main():
    print("deque-map")
    print(f"{via_deque_map()}")
    print("end")
